{"audit_run_id":"audit:c34cc885ef2f4624ab5a3d25a51b98ed","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":33,"end_line":3,"start_column":1,"start_line":3,"text":"File: `aphasia_therapy_data.csv`"},{"end_column":77,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"One row is one participant in the service evaluation: one adult with chronic"},{"end_column":82,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"post-stroke aphasia, four to twelve months after a single left-hemisphere stroke,"},{"end_column":77,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"allocated to one of the two therapy schedules and assessed once by a blinded"},{"end_column":71,"end_line":10,"start_column":1,"start_line":10,"text":"assessor at the end of therapy. Each participant appears exactly once."},{"end_column":74,"end_line":12,"start_column":1,"start_line":12,"text":"The file holds a header row plus 54 participant rows: 27 allocated to the"},{"end_column":74,"end_line":13,"start_column":1,"start_line":13,"text":"intensive schedule and 27 to the distributed schedule. Rows are listed in"},{"end_column":77,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"allocation order, so the two schedules are interleaved. There are no missing"},{"end_column":72,"end_line":15,"start_column":1,"start_line":15,"text":"cells and no extra rows; every participant has a value in every column."},{"end_column":28,"end_line":19,"start_column":1,"start_line":19,"text":"| Column | Type | Meaning |"},{"end_column":20,"end_line":20,"start_column":1,"start_line":20,"text":"| --- | --- | --- |"},{"end_column":148,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"| `participant_id` | text | Participant identifier: the prefix `P` plus a zero-padded serial number, `P01` through `P54`. Unique across the file. |"},{"end_column":207,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"| `group` | text | Therapy schedule the participant was allocated to. Exactly two distinct values: `intensive` (15 hours per week for 3 weeks) and `distributed` (the same total hours spread over 9 weeks). |"},{"end_column":306,"end_line":23,"start_column":1,"start_line":23,"text":"| `naming_accuracy_pct` | number | Picture-naming accuracy at the end of therapy, as a percentage of the 60 test items named correctly. Recorded as a whole number of items correct and reported as a percentage to one decimal place, so values are multiples of 1/60 of 100 percent. Possible range 0 to 100. |"},{"end_column":140,"end_line":24,"start_column":1,"start_line":24,"text":"| `speech_rate_wpm` | number | Connected-speech rate in the standard picture-description task, in words per minute, to one decimal place. |"},{"end_column":218,"end_line":25,"start_column":1,"start_line":25,"text":"| `functional_communication_0_100` | integer | Functional communication in everyday life, rated by a familiar communication partner on a 0 to 100 scale, whole points only. Higher means better everyday communication. |"},{"end_column":72,"end_line":27,"start_column":1,"start_line":27,"text":"The three outcome columns appear in the order declared in the protocol:"},{"end_column":75,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"picture naming, then connected-speech rate, then functional communication."},{"end_column":79,"end_line":32,"start_column":1,"start_line":32,"text":"- Units follow how each measure is taken: naming accuracy comes from a 60-item"},{"end_column":69,"end_line":33,"start_column":3,"start_line":33,"text":"test, speech rate from a timed picture description, and functional"},{"end_column":55,"end_line":34,"start_column":3,"start_line":34,"text":"communication from a partner-completed rating scale."},{"end_column":81,"end_line":35,"start_column":1,"start_line":35,"text":"- Values are fixed and committed to the CSV. `make_data.py` in this directory is"},{"end_column":77,"end_line":36,"start_column":3,"start_line":36,"text":"the one-off authoring script that produced the file; it is not part of the"},{"end_column":46,"end_line":37,"start_column":3,"start_line":37,"text":"analysis and does not need to be run again."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:c6227e35d8b1ff133945","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:ee3b62ab659f352ae558288d36e4d5aebab52bfed7f5b22d3db8b3d3ce7d470e","end_line":37,"locator":"DATA_DESCRIPTION.md:1-37","path":"DATA_DESCRIPTION.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
{"audit_run_id":"audit:c34cc885ef2f4624ab5a3d25a51b98ed","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":97,"end_line":3,"start_column":1,"start_line":3,"text":"This study compares the two groups recorded in the `group` column of `aphasia_therapy_data.csv`."},{"end_column":128,"end_line":4,"start_column":1,"start_line":4,"text":"The pre-declared outcome family, in this fixed order, is: naming_accuracy_pct, speech_rate_wpm, functional_communication_0_100."},{"end_column":85,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"Each outcome is compared between the two groups. The named outcomes form one outcome"},{"end_column":88,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"family; per-outcome comparisons over this family require complete-family control of the"},{"end_column":45,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"family-wise error from multiple comparisons."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:88bef9f72f04878b7002","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:bcbaa877016063f7554dc69f243d1dfff4dcfe2fb50b610b08a282f1e26ae1dc","end_line":7,"locator":"PROTOCOL.md:1-7","path":"PROTOCOL.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
